<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/inspection-visit.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/inspection-visit-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/inspection-visit.webp 1021w" sizes="100vw" width="1021" height="681" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/nh-claim-calculators/">Calculators</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Claim File Readiness Gauge</span></nav><p class="kicker">Free checklist</p><h1>Appraisal Readiness Checklist and Score</h1><p class="lede">Appraisals are won by the file you bring to them. Answer twelve quick questions to see what’s solid and what still needs work.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec sec-tool"><div class="wrap"><h2 class="sr-only">Claim File Readiness Gauge</h2><div class="rv">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Claim file readiness gauge</span><i>12 questions · two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the claim was denied, speak with a New Hampshire attorney before thinking about appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask in writing for the complete line-item estimate, including the roof diagram or measurement report."><span>Do you have the insurer’s full, itemized estimate — not just a summary page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an independent line-item estimate. A one-line lump-sum bid rarely holds up in front of a panel."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate from a contractor or estimator?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Pull every photo you have, note when each was taken and add current-condition photos."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Appraisal’ condition and note the time limits for naming an appraiser."><span>Have you read the Appraisal paragraph in your policy conditions?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Read the ‘Suit Against Us’ condition and put the date on a calendar — the Granite State claim clock can help."><span>Do you know your policy’s suit-limitation date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Finish reasonable temporary repairs and keep every receipt and invoice."><span>Were temporary repairs made (tarps, water extraction, heat restored) and receipts kept?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request your declarations page from your agent or the insurer."><span>Do you have your current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure concealed areas have been inspected so the scope is complete before anyone values it."><span>Has hidden damage — attic sheathing, wet insulation, wall cavities — been opened and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Collect emails, letters and claim-portal messages in one folder, oldest first."><span>Is your correspondence with the insurer saved in date order?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the dispute size & net recovery estimator. A small gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap between estimates more than roughly 10% or $5,000?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="If a proof of loss was requested, return it within the stated time."><span>If the insurer asked for a sworn proof of loss, was it sent on time?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Clear answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out tool-out-score" aria-live="polite">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#e8eefb" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#efae0e" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul data-o="todo" class="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div>
<p class="hint center">For planning only. Results depend on what you enter and your policy terms, and aren’t a quote, appraisal or legal advice. Nothing is stored.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>How the questions are weighted</h2>
<p>Coverage, estimates and evidence count most because they decide whether appraisal fits at all and how well your number will hold up. Paperwork items still matter, but they’re quicker to fix.</p>
<h2>What the score means</h2>
<ul><li><strong>75 or higher:</strong> a well-built file. A professional review of the gap is a sensible next step.</li>
<li><strong>45 to 74:</strong> close the open items first.</li>
<li><strong>Under 45:</strong> demanding appraisal now could lock in a low number.</li></ul>

<h2>About this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is anything I click saved?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. The checklist runs in your browser and nothing is stored or sent.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I bring the result to a consultation?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Take a screenshot of your score and to-do list.</p></div></details></div>
